      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T00:04:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good to know! Unfortunately I couldn\u0027t figure out a way to get it to return the `binder::Result`. In the last part of that link it sounds like we might still need to anyhow to return a different error type?\n\n```\nIf returning an error type which does need to be lifted via anyhow!, feel free to continue to use direct return statements.\n```\nWith the suggested change I see:\n```\nerror[E0308]: mismatched types\n    --\u003e packages/modules/Virtualization/android/virtmgr/src/aidl.rs:1413:9\n     |\n1413 |         ensure!(matches!(\u0026*self.instance.vm_state.lock().unwrap(), VmState::Running { .. }), \"VM is not running\")\n     |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `Status`, found `Error`\n     |\n     \u003d note: this error originates in the macro `$crate::__anyhow` which comes from the expansion of the macro `ensure` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)\n\nerror[E0599]: no method named `or_service_specific_exception` found for unit type `()` in the current scope\n    --\u003e packages/modules/Virtualization/android/virtmgr/src/aidl.rs:1414:2\n     |\n1413 | /         ensure!(matches!(\u0026*self.instance.vm_state.lock().unwrap(), VmState::Running { .. }), \"VM is not running\")\n1414 | | .or_service_specific_exception(-1)?;\n     | | -^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ method not found in `()`\n     | |_|\n     |\n```\n\nDo you have any tips? I couldn\u0027t find any examples of ensure in a [binder function](https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003dbinder::status%20f:rs$%20%22ensure!%22\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main%20-f:prebuilts).\n\nI need to read up more on that anyhow crate anyways! 😊\n\nThis pattern was copy/pasted from above in `connectVsock()`. There are a lot other instances of `return Err(anyhow...` in `modules/Virtualization`.",
      "parentUuid": "7bb9a2b4_e6e880a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1410,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1411,
